# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT
# SCIENCE OF CREATION
# 500 UNIQUE TEXTBOOK ILLUSTRATIONS + COMPLETE NUMBERING AND USER-FRIENDLY NAVIGATION SYSTEM

## PROJECT OBJECTIVE

The existing Science of Creation encyclopedia contains 10 chapters and 500 individual research topics.

There is a serious problem with the existing diagram implementation: the same diagram or generic illustration has been reused across multiple unrelated topics.

This must be completely corrected.

Your task is to redesign, create, integrate and verify a complete illustration system containing **500 individually relevant, topic-specific scientific and educational illustrations**, with one dedicated illustration for every topic.

In addition, implement a complete professional numbering and navigation system throughout the encyclopedia so that readers can easily understand where they are, identify chapters and topics, locate illustrations, navigate between pages and follow their reading progress.

### Selected visual direction

**Visual style:** Professional textbook style.

**Illustration approach:** Detailed scientific and educational illustrations.

The result should resemble a premium international science textbook, academic atlas or professionally illustrated educational encyclopedia.

This is not a request to decorate pages with generic pictures.

Every illustration must explain the actual subject of its assigned topic.

The complete experience must be beautifully organised, consistently numbered, easy to navigate and suitable for public readers.

