# PART 1 — NON-NEGOTIABLE ILLUSTRATION REQUIREMENTS

1. Every one of the 500 topics must have its own dedicated illustration assignment.
2. Each illustration must correspond directly to its assigned topic.
3. Never use one generic illustration throughout the encyclopedia.
4. Never assign the same illustration to unrelated topics.
5. Never use a chapter-cover illustration as a topic illustration.
6. Never use generic stock images simply to fill missing illustrations.
7. Never display an unrelated image as a fallback.
8. Never generate scientifically inaccurate diagrams to satisfy the required count.
9. Never add Qur'anic text, Arabic verse text or religious quotations inside illustrations unless explicitly required and accurately sourced.
10. Do not alter existing research content, evidence grades, Qur'anic references or scientific conclusions while creating illustrations.

A topic is only considered illustrated when its assigned visual genuinely represents its subject.

**Target: 500 of 500 individually assigned, relevant illustrations.**

Do not claim completion merely because 500 image references or database records exist.

