# PART 3 — CREATE A UNIQUE ILLUSTRATION FOR EVERY TOPIC

Work through all 10 chapters and all 500 topics.

For each topic:

1. Read the complete topic title.
2. Read its scientific topic.
3. Read its scientific finding.
4. Read its scientific explanation.
5. Read its limitations.
6. Understand what the topic actually describes.
7. Identify the most useful visual explanation.
8. Design an illustration specifically for that topic.
9. Add accurate labels and annotations.
10. Write a topic-specific caption.
11. Integrate the illustration into the correct topic page.
12. Verify that the illustration is actually displayed on that page.

Do not design illustrations from titles alone when the scientific explanation provides more precise information.

The illustration must represent the actual scientific subject, not simply a keyword appearing in the title.

